#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"A process has a log priority mask that determines which calls to "
"B<syslog>(3)  may be logged.  All other calls will be ignored.  Logging is "
"enabled for the priorities that have the corresponding bit set in I<mask>.  "
"The initial mask is such that logging is enabled for all priorities."
msgstr ""
"Chaque processus a un masque de priorité déterminant quels appels à "
"B<syslog>(3) seront effectivement journalisés. Les autres appels seront "
"ignorés. La journalisation est activée pour les priorités ayant un bit "
"correspondant dans le I<masque>. Le masque initial valide toutes les "
"priorités."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
#: opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<setlogmask>()  function sets this logmask for the calling process, and "
"returns the previous mask.  If the I<mask> argument is B<0>, the current "
"logmask is not modified."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<setlogmask>() définit le masque des priorités pour le "
"processus appelant et renvoie le masque précédent. Si l'argument I<masque> "
"est B<0>, le masque en cours n'est pas modifié."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The eight priorities are B<LOG_EMERG>, B<LOG_ALERT>, B<LOG_CRIT>, "
"B<LOG_ERR>, B<LOG_WARNING>, B<LOG_NOTICE>, B<LOG_INFO>, and B<LOG_DEBUG>.  "
"The bit corresponding to a priority I<p> is I<LOG_MASK(p)>.  Some systems "
"also provide a macro I<LOG_UPTO(p)> for the mask of all priorities in the "
"above list up to and including I<p>."
msgstr ""
"Les huit priorités sont B<LOG_EMERG>, B<LOG_ALERT>, B<LOG_CRIT>, B<LOG_ERR>, "
"B<LOG_WARNING>, B<LOG_NOTICE>, B<LOG_INFO> et B<LOG_DEBUG>. Le bit "
"correspondant à la priorité I<p> est I<LOG_MASK>(p). Certains systèmes "
"fournissent aussi une macro I<LOG_UPTO>(p) pour le masque de toutes les "
"priorités jusqu'à I<p> incluses."

